---
import { url } from '../../config';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import DemoBadge from '../../components/DemoBadge.astro';
---
<Base title="Example Mini PC for a first homelab (demo review)" description="Sample NeonKey review layout for a first homelab mini PC: who it's for, pros and cons, a plain verdict and affiliate disclosure.">
  <article class="narrow page-head prose">
    <div class="disclosure" role="note">
      <strong>Affiliate disclosure:</strong> NeonKey may earn a commission if you buy through links on this page, at no extra cost to you. It doesn't change the verdict. <a href={url('/disclosure/')}>Full disclosure</a>.
    </div>
    <span class="kicker">Review · Homelab hardware</span>
    <h1>Example Mini PC for a first homelab</h1>
    <div class="meta"><DemoBadge /><span>Placeholder product, not a real review</span><span>·</span><span>No rating shown in demo</span></div>

    <div class="placeholder-art" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">Product image placeholder</div>

    <h2>Who it's for</h2>
    <p>Beginners who want a quiet, low-power box to run a few containers (like n8n, a DNS filter or a media server) without repurposing their main computer.</p>

    <h2>What I'd check before buying</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>RAM: can it be upgraded, and to how much?</li>
      <li>Storage: is there room for a second drive?</li>
      <li>Networking: wired Ethernet speed, and does Linux support the NIC well?</li>
      <li>Power draw and noise if it's running 24/7</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="proscons">
      <div class="pros">
        <h3>Pros (placeholder)</h3>
        <ul><li>Small and quiet</li><li>Low power for always-on use</li><li>Enough for several light containers</li></ul>
      </div>
      <div class="cons">
        <h3>Cons (placeholder)</h3>
        <ul><li>Limited upgrade room</li><li>Not for heavy virtualization</li><li>Fan noise varies by unit</li></ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="verdict">
      <span class="kicker">Verdict</span>
      <p style="margin:.4rem 0 0"><strong>Placeholder verdict:</strong> a sensible first homelab box if your goals are learning and light self-hosting. If you want many VMs, look at something with more RAM headroom. Real verdicts will only be written after hands-on testing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="buy-box" aria-labelledby="buy-h">
      <h2 id="buy-h" style="margin-top:0;font-size:1.25rem">Where to buy</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="font-size:.92rem">Demo links: these go nowhere. Prices aren't shown because they change; check the retailer.</p>
      <div class="buy-row"><span>Retailer A</span><a class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" href="#" rel="sponsored nofollow" data-umami-event="affiliate-click" data-umami-event-item="example-mini-pc" data-umami-event-retailer="retailer-a">Check price</a></div>
      <div class="buy-row"><span>Retailer B</span><a class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" href="#" rel="sponsored nofollow" data-umami-event="affiliate-click" data-umami-event-item="example-mini-pc" data-umami-event-retailer="retailer-b">Check price</a></div>
    </div>

    <p><a href={url('/reviews/')}>← Back to Reviews</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
